# TopEdge marketing copy (non-negotiable)

When writing or editing marketing pages, heroes, feature blocks, CTAs, or SEO titles:

## Never use

- Em dashes (`—`). Use a comma, period, or rewrite the sentence.
- Filler eyebrows like `WhatsApp growth OS · Shopify India`, `CART RECOVERY` all-caps labels that restate the H1, or `Built for Indian D2C operators`.
- Duplicate brand in the hero when the logo is already in the navbar (no second `TopEdge` wordmark under the logo).
- Trust-pill rows under CTAs (`No credit card`, `You approve every template`, `Meta utility ~₹0.13/msg`, `Native OAuth sync`, `~15 minutes to live`, etc.). Put facts in body copy or pricing only when needed.
- Sample / illustrative toast spam on the homepage unless the user asks.
- Long stacked bullet lists in the first viewport of a homepage feature block (Instantly pattern: headline + one short sentence + CTA + visual).

## Always do

- Crisp, short sentences. Benefit first. No hype adjectives.
- Wider subheads (generous `max-width`) so copy sits on fewer lines and less height.
- Homepage: only the few stories that matter. Deep hubs live on `/features/*`.
- Instantly-style feature blocks: centered title + short body + CTA, then a unique scene (not the same card layout for every section).
- Scene UI may use middots (`·`) for compact product labels inside mocks. Marketing headlines and body copy should avoid middot slogan stacks.

## Hero template

```
H1: one clear line (no em dash)
Sub: 1–2 short sentences, max-width ~42rem
CTAs: primary + optional secondary
Visual: FeatureScene
```

## If unsure

Cut the line. Prefer silence over filler.
